    "title": "Coachella 2026 Resale Ticket Prices Are Soaring, But Weekend 2 Is Much Cheaper – Best Options Revealed!",
    "text": "The 2026 Coachella Music Festival will be starting in just a matter of hours and if you want last-minute tickets, they’re going to cost you a lot of money. Luckily, there are two weekends of the festival and the second weekend is a lot cheaper at the moment. Sabrina Carpenter, Justin Bieber, and Karol G are headlining the music festival in the desert across two weekends this month, April 10-12 and April 17-19. If you bought your tickets during the regular sale, you could have scored a weekend one general admission pass for $649 for the full weekend or a weekend two general admission pass for $549 for the full weekend. VIP passes went for $1,299 for weekend one and $1,199 for weekend two. Well, if you want to attend still, you’ll be paying a LOT more than that. Keep reading to find out more… Coachella’s official website has some resale options, but there are also tickets available on major resale sites like Stubhub and Vivid Seats. As of Thursday, April 9 at 4pm PT, here are the best prices. These prices will continue to fluctuate as tickets are sold and more passes are added: WEEKEND ONE STUBHUB: $2,905 for GA or $5,061 for VIP VIVID SEATS: $3,218 for GA or $4,376 for VIP WEEKEND TWO STUBHUB: $1,266 for GA or $2,075 for VIP VIVID SEATS: $1,313 for GA or $2,539 for VIP Disclosure: Some products on this site use affiliate links and we may earn commission for any purchase made through the links.",
